            "body": "## Code Review\n\nThis pull request modifies the weight loading logic in the compressed_tensors_w8a16_fp8 scheme to transpose weights to (K, N) format, ensuring the Marlin kernel correctly identifies the layout for square matrices. The review feedback points out that the .contiguous() call added during the transpose is redundant and inefficient, as the Marlin repacking process already handles layout and contiguity; removing it would reduce peak memory usage during model loading.",
            "comments": {
              "nodes": [
                {
                  "author": {
                    "__typename": "Bot",
                    "login": "gemini-code-assist"
                  },
                  "body": "![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nWhile the transpose is necessary to fix the layout detection for square matrices in the Marlin kernel, calling `.contiguous()` here is redundant and inefficient. The Marlin repacking process (specifically `pack_fp8_to_int32` called within `prepare_fp8_layer_for_marlin`) already handles transposing the weight back to its original (N, K) layout and ensuring contiguity. By passing a non-contiguous view (`.t()`) here, you avoid creating an intermediate full-weight copy that would be immediately discarded and re-copied later, saving significant peak memory during model loading.\n\n```suggestion\n            replace_parameter(layer, \"weight\", layer.weight.t())\n```",
                  "createdAt": "2026-05-14T16:09:28Z",
                  "databaseId": 3242670300,
                  "diffHunk": "@@ -137,6 +137,12 @@ def process_weights_after_loading(self, layer: torch.nn.Module) -> None:\n                     \"weight_scale\",\n                     convert_to_channelwise(layer.weight_scale, layer.logical_widths),\n                 )\n+            # Weights are loaded in (N, K) format from the checkpoint.\n+            # Transpose to (K, N) here so the Marlin kernel's shape-based\n+            # heuristic (which skips the transpose when it sees (K, N)) works\n+            # correctly even for square weight matrices where (N, K) == (K, N)\n+            # in shape but not in value.\n+            replace_parameter(layer, \"weight\", layer.weight.t().contiguous())",
                  "line": 145,
                  "originalLine": 145,
                  "path": "vllm/model_executor/layers/quantization/compressed_tensors/schemes/compressed_tensors_w8a16_fp8.py",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-05-14T16:09:28Z",
                  "url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/42657#discussion_r3242670300"
                }
