      "changes": 6,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/contents/vllm%2Fmodel_executor%2Flayers%2Fquantization%2Fcompressed_tensors%2Fschemes%2Fcompressed_tensors_w8a16_fp8.py?ref=906b1f92edf51398e2f22922b15085ed7f8c1609",
      "deletions": 0,
      "filename": "vllm/model_executor/layers/quantization/compressed_tensors/schemes/compressed_tensors_w8a16_fp8.py",
      "patch": "@@ -137,6 +137,12 @@ def process_weights_after_loading(self, layer: torch.nn.Module) -> None:\n                     \"weight_scale\",\n                     convert_to_channelwise(layer.weight_scale, layer.logical_widths),\n                 )\n+            # Weights are loaded in (N, K) format from the checkpoint.\n+            # Transpose to (K, N) here so the Marlin kernel's shape-based\n+            # heuristic (which skips the transpose when it sees (K, N)) works\n+            # correctly even for square weight matrices where (N, K) == (K, N)\n+            # in shape but not in value.\n+            replace_parameter(layer, \"weight\", layer.weight.t().contiguous())\n \n         self.linear_kernel.process_weights_after_loading(layer)\n ",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/raw/906b1f92edf51398e2f22922b15085ed7f8c1609/vllm%2Fmodel_executor%2Flayers%2Fquantization%2Fcompressed_tensors%2Fschemes%2Fcompressed_tensors_w8a16_fp8.py",
      "sha": "bf8101d32483545c0740d46666a7f9b8a22f9d66",
      "status": "modified"
    }
  ],
  "inline_comments": [
    {
      "body": "![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nWhile the transpose is necessary to fix the layout detection for square matrices in the Marlin kernel, calling `.contiguous()` here is redundant and inefficient. The Marlin repacking process (specifically `pack_fp8_to_int32` called within `prepare_fp8_layer_for_marlin`) already handles transposing the weight back to its original (N, K) layout and ensuring contiguity. By passing a non-contiguous view (`.t()`) here, you avoid creating an intermediate full-weight copy that would be immediately discarded and re-copied later, saving significant peak memory during model loading.\n\n```suggestion\n            replace_parameter(layer, \"weight\", layer.weight.t())\n```",
      "created_at": "2026-05-14T16:09:28Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -137,6 +137,12 @@ def process_weights_after_loading(self, layer: torch.nn.Module) -> None:\n                     \"weight_scale\",\n                     convert_to_channelwise(layer.weight_scale, layer.logical_widths),\n                 )\n+            # Weights are loaded in (N, K) format from the checkpoint.\n+            # Transpose to (K, N) here so the Marlin kernel's shape-based\n+            # heuristic (which skips the transpose when it sees (K, N)) works\n+            # correctly even for square weight matrices where (N, K) == (K, N)\n+            # in shape but not in value.\n+            replace_parameter(layer, \"weight\", layer.weight.t().contiguous())",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/42657#discussion_r3242670300",
      "id": 3242670300,
